// RX data-batch illustration only; no RTL interface or clock-phase guarantee.
// Display FRAME_CNT, ROW_CNT, COL_CNT and DATA_RX only.
// Fixed color by scale: FRAME blue (5), ROW purple (8), COL green (7), DATA white (2).
// DATA labels F/R/i identify the current frame, row and zero-based batch.
// COL_CNT is shown symbolically as i*128, i=0..95 (96 batches per row).
// Pixel index = ROW_CNT*12288 + i*128 + lane, lane=0..127; reset numbering each frame.
// After batch 95: COL_CNT=0*128 and ROW_CNT increments; after row 12287,
// ROW_CNT=0 and FRAME_CNT increments. Counter widths/overflow are not specified.
// Show rows 0,1,12287: first three batches and batch 95; then next-frame first batch.
// Aligned | slots 3/8/14 omit batches 3..94 (92 batches); slot 10 omits rows 2..12286.
// Inter-row/inter-frame intervals are omitted, not asserted to be zero.
// Compressed horizontal axis is not proportional to elapsed time.
// Compact native JsonML labels: F/R/i above DATA box; {Pfirst…Plast} inside.
// One unnamed spacer separates the DATA metadata from the COL track; four named signals remain.
{
